A||||5||gtsonly||Need help installing the distributer-Please!!!!||||5||
Z||000000||gtsonly||12-23-2001||07:50 PM||||Well, I have rebuilt the engine and the last thing I need to do is install the distributer but I am having big problems. I am reading the haynes manual about installing the distributer after the crank has been moved. I cant seem to get it in the right spot, the engine turns over but all I smell is gas. Can anyone help?????<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/myfiero001_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||GTDude||12-23-2001||08:01 PM||||sure......stick your finger in the #1 sparkplug hole....first one on the right towards the back of car.....have someone help you "bump" it over lil by lil til you feel compression.  Then line up the mark on harmonic balancer TDC with the pointer on the timing cover.  Then point the rotor to the #1 sparkplug wire on the dist. cap and drop the dist. into the hole.  You may have to move it around a bit to get it to go all the way down.  Good luck!<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||gtsonly||12-23-2001||08:04 PM||||Thats what I have been doing and still nothing. There are three marks on the Harmonic balancer??????????????? Do I bring the piston all the way to the top? Or when i start to feel compression line up the distributer?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/myfiero001_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||12-23-2001||08:26 PM||||The piston s/b up but remember it comes up twice (compression is the one you want). You may have it 180 degrees out of whack. Easy to do.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bill Shenefelt||12-23-2001||09:08 PM||||First be sure the #1 cyl is at top dead center on the compression stroke(finger over plug hole to feel compression)  Then when you seat the distributor you will see that the rotor moves a little due to gear engagement.  Reseat it as necessary to get the rotor to the #1 plug wire.  Do a static adjustment of the distributor to just fire at the timing mark and try to start it then.  You will need to get the computer out of the circuit(jumper wire in the fitting under the cigarette lighter plastic cover- I think it is the first two sockets on the passengers side, but it has been a while since I set my timing--a bent paper clip works well) and then use a timing light to tweak it into spec. <BR>Most manuals(including haynes) seem to be written by someone who has never seen the car.  Many garages(dealers) seem even worse.  Good luck.<BR>Bill Shenefelt||||reg||1
Z||000005||crgkstnr||12-23-2001||11:28 PM||||There are three marks on the Harmonic balancer??????????????? <P>GT, one of the three marks is wider (2.8v6), thats the one to use.  Mark it with paint or chalk so it will show up in the timing light.<BR>Craig<P>||||reg||1
